# {KJ|NAMESPACE}

`{KJ|GEM_NAME}` is a compatibility shim for `{KJ|SHIMMED_GEM_NAME}`.

New applications should depend on `{KJ|SHIMMED_GEM_NAME}` directly. This gem exists so existing applications that still depend on `{KJ|GEM_NAME}` can load the replacement implementation without changing all require paths at once.

## Installation

```ruby
gem "{KJ|GEM_NAME}"
```

## Runtime behavior

Loading this gem requires `{KJ|SHIMMED_REQUIRE}` and leaves implementation behavior to `{KJ|SHIMMED_GEM_NAME}`.

The generated compatibility require paths are:

```text
{KJ|SHIM_COMPAT_REQUIRES}
```

## Migration

When you are ready to remove the compatibility layer, replace `{KJ|GEM_NAME}` with `{KJ|SHIMMED_GEM_NAME}` in your dependency list and require `{KJ|SHIMMED_REQUIRE}` directly.
